cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ChainFL-RA: Blockchain-Enabled Decentralized Federated Learning with Reputation-Weighted Robust Aggregation and On-Chain Auditable Incentives"
message: "If you use this software or its experimental artifacts, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Song
    affiliation: School of Electrical and Information Engineering, Tianjin University; Institute of Applied Mathematics, Hebei Academy of Sciences
  - family-names: Jin
    given-names: Zhigang
    affiliation: School of Electrical and Information Engineering, Tianjin University
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Zhiqiang
    affiliation: Institute of Applied Mathematics, Hebei Academy of Sciences; Information Security Authentication Technology Innovation Center of Hebei Province
repository-code: "https://github.com/tangsng/ChainFL-RA"
abstract: "ChainFL-RA unifies robust aggregation, on-chain reputation, and token settlement in decentralized federated learning under a single verifiable quality signal. Evaluated against FedAvg, Krum, FedRoLA, and FLAME on MNIST, Fashion-MNIST, and CIFAR-10 under label-flipping, update-scaling, and an adaptive Min-Max attack, it is the only method that remains robust in every setting."
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - blockchain
  - robust aggregation
  - Byzantine robustness
  - reputation system
  - smart contracts
  - incentive mechanism
